WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.180
We’ve all dreamed of world peace at one
time or another.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.620
Cynics might say that total, uninterrupted
peace on a global scale is something that

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.470
could never be achieved.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:17.099
Wars, crime, unstable political relationships,
international tension; as long as human beings

00:00:17.099 --> 00:00:22.439
have the capacity for these things, they will
remain as obstacles standing in the way of

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:23.869
world peace.

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:27.999
And then there’s all the SCPs and dangerous
anomalies out there.

00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:32.940
Just the existence of half the horrors contained
by the SCP Foundation could easily bring about

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.520
the end of the entire world as we know it,
and it’s hard to achieve peace when death

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.350
and destruction could be right around the
corner.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.329
But what if that wasn’t the case?

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:49.649
What if there was no end of the world scenario;
no evil eldritch god pulling the strings above,

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.809
and no catastrophe waiting to finally drop?

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:55.870
What if the world was just… safe?

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:00.390
If an existence of perfect peace and harmony
still sounds like a pipe dream to you, then

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:05.500
perhaps you should join us on a trip into
the unknown, a journey into a world where

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.540
things are so much better than here.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.040
Welcome to SCP-6001, welcome to Avalon.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:19.200
A safer and more peaceful world has always
been, at least partly, the goal of the SCP

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.200
Foundation.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.630
And it is true that, without their containment
and understanding of anomalous objects, the

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:29.560
world would be a far more dangerous place
- if it wasn’t completely destroyed in its

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.560
entirety.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.390
However, there is always more that the Foundation
could do with their vast resources to improve

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:36.610
the world.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.140
There are even SCPs that they have contained
whose anomalous abilities could greatly benefit

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.890
all of mankind, but the organization would
hardly ever approve of doing anything like

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.390
that, right?

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:53.590
Well, SCP-6001 is a universe in which that
actually happened, or rather something similar

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.590
happened.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:59.100
Here, the resources of an organization like
the Foundation were put to better use, and

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:05.060
ultimately created a utopia, a paradise for
all, achieving what we referred to at the

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.610
start of this video: World peace.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:13.921
The entry for SCP-6001 on the SCP Archive
opens with an email addressed to us from a

00:02:13.921 --> 00:02:18.070
member of Foundation personnel called David
Caspian, that reads:

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:22.230
“Hey, sorry, I know it's late, but I just
had to share this with someone, and there's

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.510
no one in the world I'd rather share it with
than you.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.260
I just had the most incredible day.”

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:30.830
Then, as the article continues, there are
numerous format changes from the standard

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.820
SCP Foundation entries that we’re familiar
with.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:38.280
In particular, the typical terminology is
vastly altered from what we’d be familiar

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.280
with.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.470
The term “SCP” is now “Phenom”, “Special
Containment Procedures” has been replaced

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:48.020
with “Modus”, “Imprimis” takes the
place of “Description” and even the name

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:53.070
of the organization is different: the Compendium
Phenomic Inquiry.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:58.690
This appears to be a version of the SCP Foundation
that exists in some kind of parallel universe

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.600
or alternate timeline to The Foundation that
we know.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:08.340
Phenom-6001 itself is a tiny, microscopic
singularity uncovered in the Tokyo of this

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.660
other universe’s Japan.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:15.380
This singularity is linked to another version
of Tokyo from another universe, which is referred

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.740
to as A6K.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:23.430
This universe, A6K, is described by the Compendium
as being similar to their own reality, in

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.880
almost every superficial and surface level
way.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.360
It looks the same, contains the same people,
the same places, and even the same anomalies,

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.870
but that is where the similarities end.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:39.980
The A6K universe diverges from this baseline
by having a general lack of cooperation among

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:45.220
its inhabitants, scientific repression along
with heightened paranoia, aggression, and

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.709
levels of violence.

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:48.000
Sound familiar?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:54.920
It should, because A6K’s main scientific
institution is a group known as the SCP Foundation.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.620
That’s right, A6K is the Foundation’s
reality.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:05.099
The Foundation is aware of what it refers
to as SCP-6001, but because of the tiny size

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:09.280
of the singularity that links their world
with that of the Compendium, none of their

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.730
personnel are able to travel through to that
reality.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:17.209
The Compendium states that it is considering
unifying with the Foundation, striking up

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:19.480
an alliance between universes.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.600
However, they both have dramatically different
approaches which would likely get in the way

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:24.610
of that.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:29.650
The SCP Foundation has always been shrouded
in secrecy, never revealing anything to the

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:35.090
public, often eliminating or memory wiping
anyone who witnesses an anomaly just to keep

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.659
everything under wraps.

00:04:36.659 --> 00:04:41.960
Meanwhile, in their universe, the CPI has
willingly made its documents and anomalous

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.259
information available to anyone that asks
for it.

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:50.499
In the Foundation’s reality, the world they
were linked to via SCP-6001 was seemingly

00:04:50.499 --> 00:04:55.620
first discovered when David Caspian, the personnel
member we mentioned earlier, hunched over

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.300
the spot where the singularity was located
for almost five minutes.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:03.449
He had been doing this for a number of weeks
since the Foundation’s instruments first

00:05:03.449 --> 00:05:08.220
detected the existence of the tiny hole connecting
A6K with another dimension.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:14.810
David’s focus had been so fixated on the
spot where SCP-6001 was, that it wasn’t

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:19.240
until he got back up that he realized he was
in a completely different universe.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:24.490
He described tall, rounded skyscrapers unlike
the Tokyo of the Foundation’s world, gigantic

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:28.400
ivy growing up the buildings with leaves the
size of cars.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:33.180
The clouds above had been replaced with the
clearest blue sky, and clean, fresh air took

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.150
the place of the stale, polluted environment
David had just left.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:42.800
A nearby cat was perched on the same rooftop
as David, watching strange, seed-shaped glass

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:47.699
constructs floating on the horizon, filled
with lush green innards.

00:05:47.699 --> 00:05:53.210
The cat had a coat of spotted orange, white
and brown, underneath an actual coat, a violet

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:58.520
blazer, complete with a white bow under the
collar and a black brooch pinned to it; the

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.219
shape of an eye inside a globe.

00:06:01.219 --> 00:06:03.440
It even wore a pair of spectacles.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.169
The cat, Primrose, greeted David by name and
introduced herself, the pair sharing a brief

00:06:08.169 --> 00:06:11.110
joke about “stepping through the looking
glass.”

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.259
Both of them were doctors.

00:06:12.259 --> 00:06:16.800
In fact, David was the Foundation’s Head
of Alt-Dimensional Research.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.669
When he asked Primrose how he’d arrived
on her side of SCP-6001, she responded by

00:06:21.669 --> 00:06:25.619
asking if he had heard of something called
cross-dimensional test sampling.

00:06:25.619 --> 00:06:30.120
Of course, David was more than familiar with
it, not only was it a standard procedure for

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.069
the SCP Foundation, but one that he himself
had written.

00:06:34.069 --> 00:06:38.620
The procedure involved bringing an isolated
part of another reality to a safe environment

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.569
within one’s own for testing purposes.

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:46.589
This is exactly what the Compendium had done
to bring David to their universe.

00:06:46.589 --> 00:06:51.599
According to Primrose, the Compendium had
many similar procedures to the Foundation,

00:06:51.599 --> 00:06:56.029
causing David to ask why, if this was the
case, he wasn’t being scanned or checked

00:06:56.029 --> 00:07:01.759
for contaminants and pathogens, or paralysed
to prevent kinetographic memetics.

00:07:01.759 --> 00:07:06.309
Primrose responded by simply asking if he
had eaten breakfast and seemingly inviting

00:07:06.309 --> 00:07:07.939
him to Paris.

00:07:07.939 --> 00:07:12.529
Primrose then sat with David on an armchair
on the Tokyo rooftop and spoke an address

00:07:12.529 --> 00:07:13.529
to it.

00:07:13.529 --> 00:07:18.189
The next moment, she and David were transported
to Paris, in a courtyard filled with similar

00:07:18.189 --> 00:07:22.249
chairs that other people and animals were
using to teleport.

00:07:22.249 --> 00:07:27.159
Primrose referred to them as The Everywhere
Chair, a form of public transport.

00:07:27.159 --> 00:07:34.029
David remarked that there was something similar
in the A6K universe, referring to SCP-1609,

00:07:34.029 --> 00:07:37.029
which was destroyed by the Global Occult Coalition.

00:07:37.029 --> 00:07:41.930
The cat responded by saying that David would
find many similarities between their universes

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:45.839
and mentioned that she was the Department
Head of Trans-Dimensional Development and

00:07:45.839 --> 00:07:48.080
Discovery for the CPI.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.899
But then, Primrose declared she no longer
wanted to discuss work as she was already

00:07:51.899 --> 00:07:55.800
off the clock despite it only being the early
hours of the morning.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:00.520
When David questioned this, Primrose replied
“The wonders of automation, David.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:04.220
More hands make less work, and we have a lot
of hands.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:07.929
Besides, I've something more important lined
up for today.”

00:08:07.929 --> 00:08:13.310
She then ordered Oeufs Brouillés from a holographic
menu, and David ordered the same, remarking

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:18.210
“When in Rome – or Paris – or a parallel
reality with talking cats – you do as the

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.210
Romans.”

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:24.439
David then asked Primrose about the Compendium,
learning it was a primarily scientific institute

00:08:24.439 --> 00:08:27.649
but that it lacked the employees of the SCP
Foundation.

00:08:27.649 --> 00:08:32.940
Primrose and her fellow researchers were under
no obligation to work for the CPI, but rather

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:38.409
were able to choose to work with them out
of their own curiosity or interest.

00:08:38.409 --> 00:08:43.209
The Compendium was also responsible for running
the governments, economies, and law enforcement

00:08:43.209 --> 00:08:49.269
of the entire world, with Primrose likening
the organization to “benevolent dictators”.

00:08:49.269 --> 00:08:53.589
David then expressed surprise that people
didn’t resist the Compendium taking control

00:08:53.589 --> 00:08:56.750
of the world, to which his feline counterpart
replied:

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.199
“Goodness no.

00:08:58.199 --> 00:08:59.199
Governments?

00:08:59.199 --> 00:09:00.199
Certainly.

00:09:00.199 --> 00:09:01.199
Corporations?

00:09:01.199 --> 00:09:02.199
Absolutely.

00:09:02.199 --> 00:09:03.199
The people though?

00:09:03.199 --> 00:09:04.800
Imagine a foreign power suddenly swooping
in and saying ‘Hey there.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:05.970
So, we're in charge now.

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:09.660
Here's universal healthcare, living wages,
housing, infrastructure, and total liberty

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:14.860
from anyone but us - and literally all we
ask of you is to respect basic human rights.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:15.860
That's it.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.300
We provide the rest, tax-free.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:21.959
This also includes ethically replicated BBQ,
instant global transport, and adorable talking

00:09:21.959 --> 00:09:22.959
animals.

00:09:22.959 --> 00:09:23.959
Also, the cure to cancer.’

00:09:23.959 --> 00:09:27.709
Can you really think of anyone so wedded to
existing power structures that they'd just

00:09:27.709 --> 00:09:29.320
say no to all that?”

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:34.970
It’s easy to see why people would willingly
accept something so universally beneficial.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:39.279
By the time the Compendium had gone public,
they had already been working with world governments

00:09:39.279 --> 00:09:41.829
in the shadows much like the SCP Foundation.

00:09:41.829 --> 00:09:46.810
At first, the public response had been rough,
but all it took was a few years of human life

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.680
on Earth improving to help the naysayers change
their tune.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:54.870
Partway through their meal, David and Primrose
discussed the Compendium further.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:59.149
She revealed that something called PACT-15
was currently in the process of being rolled

00:09:59.149 --> 00:10:00.899
out worldwide.

00:10:00.899 --> 00:10:07.030
PACT stood for Phenom Application and/or Combination
Technology, phenoms being the CPI’s term

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:09.290
for an SCP or anomaly.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:15.690
The initiative had come about after the Compendium
studied an Australian talking spider, or SCP-1470

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.019
as David knew it.

00:10:17.019 --> 00:10:21.660
The goal of PACTs was to find a use for phenoms
that would not only benefit the people of

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:26.120
their universe, but would also benefit the
phenoms themselves.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:30.269
These creatures, objects, and entities were
all given the freedom to choose whether or

00:10:30.269 --> 00:10:35.460
not they complied, and those that did would
find their existence to be bliss.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:40.440
David was given a tour of Primrose’s world,
encountering all manner of familiar SCPs that

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:45.970
had been repurposed and allowed to live their
best possible lives alongside human beings,

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:48.470
living in uninterrupted peace.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:53.230
For example, Dr. Clef seemingly pulled off
the impossible by finally curing 682 of its

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:56.990
aggression, shortly after finding a whole
nest of the creatures.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:02.480
682’s species, dubbed the Immortigons, have
since both proliferated and really mellowed

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:07.970
out, with the OG 682 stating that it no longer
finds humans disgusting.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:13.209
Another nightmarish anomaly from David’s
universe, SCP-173, the Sculpture, has found

00:11:13.209 --> 00:11:16.110
a new lease on life in this world, too.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:21.600
It lives in a museum, being adored by everyone
who sees it, and it uses a mere second of

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:27.060
being unseen every night to reshape itself
into a new beautiful construction.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:30.080
Turns out, a lot of its aggression merely
came from being confined.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:35.829
As a piece of art, it wanted to be looked
at and loved, not locked away and feared.

00:11:35.829 --> 00:11:40.149
Meanwhile, however, the various groups that
formed the Compendium Phenomic Inquiry were

00:11:40.149 --> 00:11:45.610
casting their votes on what was to be done
about the residents of dimension A6K; what

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:48.350
would they do about The Foundation?

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:53.110
Some among the Compendium saw the people of
their neighboring universe as prisoners, needing

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:54.140
liberation.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:59.281
Groups known as the Wanderers and the Charity
hoped to save universe A6K, to heal a world

00:11:59.281 --> 00:12:01.150
in need of their help.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:05.949
After all, this universe had the means to
cure diseases, end famines, and ultimately

00:12:05.949 --> 00:12:11.009
achieve total peace, and wanted to share their
gifts with the Foundation’s world.

00:12:11.009 --> 00:12:14.460
However, one by one opposing votes were cast.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:20.129
Other groups, like the Synthetic Assembly,
looked to how A6K treated machines like slaves,

00:12:20.129 --> 00:12:22.889
refusing them their own free agency.

00:12:22.889 --> 00:12:28.160
Another, known as the Partnership of Three
argued that A6K held no value.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:31.830
“Their natural resources deplete at a staggering
rate.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:34.149
Their labor force is sickly and untrained.

00:12:34.149 --> 00:12:38.079
Their cultural dissimilarities are… well,
laughable.

00:12:38.079 --> 00:12:43.140
We have everything they have – and what
little uniqueness they bring to market, so

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.579
to speak, isn’t worth its counter space.

00:12:45.579 --> 00:12:47.360
They wouldn’t even make a good tourist trap!

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:51.129
What kind of morbid SOB would want to visit
these “wonders" of theirs?

00:12:51.129 --> 00:12:55.779
It's all tombs and constructs of war, old
crumbling architecture where people would

00:12:55.779 --> 00:13:00.000
fight each other to the death for sport…
and who defaces a perfectly good mountain

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.760
like that with a bunch of dead people's faces!?!

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:07.680
Some of the Compendium claimed that the people
of universe A6K had to learn to overcome their

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:12.930
own adversities, rather than the easy option,
for their universe’s people coming in to

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.700
fix everything.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:20.230
Others simply claimed that A6K was just irredeemable,
its people not to be trusted.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:25.519
Finally, the vote was settled, the Compendium
would deny help to the Foundation and its

00:13:25.519 --> 00:13:29.899
universe, and would seal SCP-6001 just enough
to keep them out.

00:13:29.899 --> 00:13:34.830
But they would watch over A6K, and the day
when the people of that universe were ready

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:39.440
to come and ask for the Compendium’s help,
the day they were ready to finally know world

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.019
peace, they would be welcomed with open arms.

00:13:43.019 --> 00:13:45.790
Needless to say, that day hasn’t arrived
yet.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:50.259
We just really, really hope it does some time
soon.

00:13:50.259 --> 00:13:55.730
One person however, did get a happy ending
in this story: None other than David himself,

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:58.730
who now works blissfully in a bar in alternate
Osaka.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:03.380
We’d love to be happy for him, but frankly,
we’re a little too jealous.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:09.749
Now go check out “SCP-001 - When Day Breaks”
and “SCP-001 Ouroboros Cycle - The Full

00:14:09.749 --> 00:14:13.139
Story Compilation” for more alternate universe
craziness!

